tps://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/abs/10.1086/734093</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/03/saturday-assorted-links-499.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=saturday-assorted-links-499">Saturday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/abs/10.1086/734093</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/abs/10.1086/734093</guid><pubDate>Sat, 01 Mar 2025 16:46:45 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Subversive conversations]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/abs/10.1086/734130">https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/abs/10.1086/734130</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/03/saturday-assorted-links-499.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=saturday-assorted-links-499">Saturday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/abs/10.1086/734130</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/abs/10.1086/734130</guid><pubDate>Sat, 01 Mar 2025 16:46:45 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Insightful Bob McGrew tweet on GPT 4.5]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1010746747637788672/lOWcy5c0_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Bob McGrew (@bobmcgrewai) on X</p><p>That o1 is better than GPT-4.5 on most problems tells us that pre-training isn’t the optimal place to spend compute in 2025. There’s a lot of low-hanging fruit in reasoning still. But pre-training isn’t dead, it’s just waiting for reasoning to catch up to log-linear returns.</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/bobmcgrewai/status/1895228291981943265?s=46">https://x.com/bobmcgrewai/status/1895228291981943265?s=46</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/friday-assorted-links-510.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=friday-assorted-links-510">Friday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/bobmcgrewai/status/1895228291981943265?s=46</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/bobmcgrewai/status/1895228291981943265?s=46</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Feb 2025 16:28:53 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Andrej]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1296667294148382721/9Pr6XrPB_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Andrej Karpathy (@karpathy) on X</p><p>GPT 4.5 + interactive comparison :) Today marks the release of GPT4.5 by OpenAI. I’ve been looking forward to this for ~2 years, ever since GPT4 was released, because this release offers a qualitative measurement of the slope of improvement you get out of scaling pretraining</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/karpathy/status/1895213020982472863">https://x.com/karpathy/status/1895213020982472863</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/friday-assorted-links-510.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=friday-assorted-links-510">Friday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/karpathy/status/1895213020982472863</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/karpathy/status/1895213020982472863</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Feb 2025 16:28:53 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Women are not more Leftist,&nbsp;]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.louiseperry.co.uk/p/are-women-innately-left-wing">https://www.louiseperry.co.uk/p/are-women-innately-left-wing</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/friday-assorted-links-510.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=friday-assorted-links-510">Friday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.louiseperry.co.uk/p/are-women-innately-left-wing</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.louiseperry.co.uk/p/are-women-innately-left-wing</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Feb 2025 16:28:53 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Hot hand in Jeopar